d_genotypes":false,"quotes":["Subject II-3 died at 17 years of age because of a complicated pulmonary infection.","Sanger sequencing confirmed the variation at a homozygous status in the 3 affected subjects."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"10457851","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:27060890:1","pmid":"27060890","section":"mapping","statement":"Thevenon et al. (2016) performed homozygosity mapping in affected sibs of a consanguineous family and identified shared runs of homozygosity totaling 11 Mb on chromosomes 3 (chr3:104822019-111671862) and 10 (chr10:1372501-6029726); segregation in the third sib excluded the chromosome 10 interval.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["This approach identified 11-megabase of shared runs of homozygosity spreading from chr3:104822019-111671862 and chr10:1372501-6029726 (Hg19) (Figure 2A).","Extended familial segregation with Sanger sequencing in Subject 3 excluded one of the 2 homozygous interval"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:27060890:2","pmid":"27060890","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Thevenon et al. (2016) found that the homozygous synonymous IFT57 c.777G>A (p.Lys259Lys) variant, affecting the last base of exon 6, caused a complex splicing pattern with normal transcript plus 3 aberrant transcripts (skipping of exon 6, exons 5-6, or exons 4-6) detectable only after NMD inhibition, and reduced IFT57 mRNA in patient fibroblasts. The variant was absent from ExAC and from 50 northern Indian controls.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["The c.777G>A substitution affecting the last base of exon 6 induces a complex splicing pattern including the normal transcript (A) but also three pathological mRNAs resulting from exon(s) skipping (B, C, and D). The pathological transcripts are only detected after inhibition of the NMD pathway.","RNA isolated from the subject’s fibroblasts had significantly less IFT57 mRNA than did that of controls (Figure 2D)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:27060890:3","pmid":"27060890","section":"heterogeneity","statement":"Thevenon et al. (2016) found no causative IFT57 mutations by Sanger sequencing in 13 OFDS and 12 EVC1/EVC2-negative Ellis-van Creveld syndrome subjects, nor biallelic mutations in exome/ciliome data from 172 subjects with various ciliopathies.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Sanger sequencing for the 11 coding exon and intron boundaries of IFT57 was performed on 25 OFDS and EVCS subjects. No causative mutation was identified. Exome or ciliome data from 172 subjects with various ciliopathy phenotypes did not identify any biallelic causative mutations."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:27060890:4","pmid":"27060890","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Thevenon et al. (2016) showed that patient fibroblasts had normal primary cilia number and length but decreased IFT57 staining at the ciliary tip (35% vs 90% in controls) with increased basal body staining, indicating defective anterograde ciliary transport. SAG stimulation produced poor GLI1 induction in patient fibroblasts, and siRNA knockdown of IFT57 in control fibroblasts abolished GLI1 induction, indicating impaired SHH signaling.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["In the subject’s fibroblasts, staining of the ciliary tip with IFT57 was significantly decreased (90% versus 35%; p<0.001) while staining of the basal body of the primary cilium was significantly increased (p<0.01).","Stimulation of the SHH pathway by Smoothened Agonist (SAG) showed poor induction of Gli1 mRNA expression in fibroblasts from the IFT57-mutated subject compared with control fibroblasts (Figure 3C).","no induction of Gli1 mRNA expression was observed in siRNA IFT57-transfected cells"],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:27060890:5","pmid":"27060890","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Thevenon et al. (2016) reclassified the family, originally reported as an OFDS-EVCS overlap, as an unclassified OFDS with skeletal dysplasia, as the patients lacked rib shortening or thoracic narrowing but had short stature, brachymesophalangia, and stocky femoral necks.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["Indeed, the reported subjects did not present rib shortening or thorax narrowness/deformity, but displayed a short stature, brachymesophalangia and stocky femoral necks, which suggests a new OFDS subtype with skeletal dysplasia."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:10457851:1","pmid":"10457851","section":"description","statement":"Phadke et al. (1999) described a new variety of oral-facial-digital syndrome associated with acromelic short stature and genu valgum, features that overlap with Ellis-van Creveld syndrome.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Here, we report a consanguineous family with a new variety of OFDS associated with acromelic short stature and genu valgum; the features overlapping with Ellis Van Creveld syndrome."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["IFT57"],"confirmed":["IFT57"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}